From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: subarr-subgen <subarr@localhost>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:10:59 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] 0059: bump patch rev to v4.35

Patch 0058 (#77): a model load that fails with CUDA OOM no longer leaves the
VRAM it had allocated held by CTranslate2's async memory pool on an idle
server. On a failed load subgen synchronises, trims the pool to zero and logs
the pool size before and after.

The same rebuild picks up the outstanding jammy-security packages (#78).
Measured inside the published 2026.08.1-r14 (digest 0309570e) on 2026-10-18:
15 upgradable, 10 from the security pocket (curl, libcurl4, libfreetype6,
libpng16-16, libsystemd0, libudev1, libx11-6, libx11-data, libx11-xcb1,
libxml2).
---
 subgen.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/subgen.py b/subgen.py
index ab9e5f3..06c9b10 100644
--- a/subgen.py
+++ b/subgen.py
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@ subgen_version = '2026.08.1'
 # [v4.3 PATCH] subarr-subgen patch-stack revision, surfaced via /queue so subarr
 # can detect our extended capabilities (audio_language_override, etc.) and
 # degrade gracefully against vanilla mccloud/subgen which lacks them.
-subarr_subgen_patch_rev = 'v4.34'
+subarr_subgen_patch_rev = 'v4.35'
 
